WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.407
Long and wide are not quality levels.

00:00:02.407 --> 00:00:05.387
They are different ways to arrange information.

00:00:05.387 --> 00:00:09.502
Long data usually stores categories as row values.

00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:13.912
Wide data turns selected category values into columns.

00:00:13.912 --> 00:00:17.797
The dangerous part is that many pivots also aggregate.

00:00:17.797 --> 00:00:23.792
When several source rows map to one pivot cell, detail may be permanently removed.

00:00:23.792 --> 00:00:30.022
Connect this idea to a machine-learning workflow converting wide measurements into tidy long data.

00:00:30.022 --> 00:00:35.647
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:43.292
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:43.292 --> 00:00:49.077
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.077 --> 00:00:54.665
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
